-- Sale of Goods Act 1979 (Singapore), 2020 RE, informal consolidation in force from 1/4/2022.
-- LAYER 1: INTERPRETATION (s 61).  Each defined term of s 61(1) is a function: it answers "is this thing within
-- the term?".  A term the Act says it "means" is closed: a thing outside the words is JUST FALSE.  A term the Act says
-- it "includes" is open: a thing outside the named kinds is NOTHING.  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- s 61(1) says the definitions apply "unless the context otherwise requires"; that qualifier is carried by the
-- fork register (the caller decides when the context requires otherwise), not by a parameter on every function.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `soga-nouns`

DECLARE `Kind of thing asked about under the term goods` IS ONE OF
    `a personal chattel other than a thing in action or money`
    `emblements`
    `industrial growing crops`
    `a thing attached to or forming part of the land which is agreed to be severed before sale or under the contract of sale`
    `an undivided share in goods`
    `a thing in action`
    `money`
    `some other thing`

§ `Interpretation (s 61)`

§§ `The terms defined in section 61(1)`

-- s 61(1), the lead-in: the definitions apply unless the context otherwise requires.
-- src:1519 | 61.—(1) In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires —
@ref s 61(1) lead-in (src:1519)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the definitions of this section apply` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the context otherwise requires`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "unless" is read as the text's no when the context otherwise requires.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 61(1) "action".
-- src:1521 | “action” includes counterclaim and set-off;
@ref s 61(1) action (src:1521)
GIVEN `the proceeding is an action in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is a counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is a set-off` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the proceeding is an action` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the proceeding is an action in the ordinary sense` OR `the proceeding is a counterclaim` OR `the proceeding is a set-off`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“action” includes counterclaim and set-off" -- the list is not closed.
            NOTHING

-- s 61(1) "bulk".
-- src:1523 | “bulk” means a mass or collection of goods of the same kind
-- src:1524 | which —
-- src:1526 | (a) is contained in a defined space or area; and
-- src:1528 | (b) is such that any goods in the bulk are interchangeable
-- src:1529 | with any other goods therein of the same number or
-- src:1530 | quantity;
@ref s 61(1) bulk (src:1523-1530)
GIVEN `it is a mass or collection of goods of the same kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is contained in a defined space or area` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any goods in it are interchangeable with any other goods therein of the same number or quantity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the mass or collection is a bulk` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a mass or collection of goods of the same kind` AND `it is contained in a defined space or area` AND `any goods in it are interchangeable with any other goods therein of the same number or quantity`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“bulk” means a mass or collection of goods of the same kind which (a) is contained in a defined space or area; and (b) is such that any goods in the bulk are interchangeable with any other goods therein of the same number or quantity"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 61(1) "business".
-- src:1532 | “business” includes a profession and the activities of any
-- src:1533 | Government department or local or public authority;
@ref s 61(1) business (src:1532-1533)
GIVEN `the activity is a trade or ordinary business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is a profession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is the activities of a Government department or a local or public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the activity is a business` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the activity is a trade or ordinary business` OR `the activity is a profession` OR `the activity is the activities of a Government department or a local or public authority`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“business” includes a profession and the activities of any Government department or local or public authority" -- the list is not closed.
            NOTHING

-- s 61(1) "buyer".
-- src:1535 | “buyer” means a person who buys or agrees to buy goods;
@ref s 61(1) buyer (src:1535)
GIVEN `the person buys goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person agrees to buy goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the person is a buyer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person buys goods` OR `the person agrees to buy goods`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“buyer” means a person who buys or agrees to buy goods"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 61(1) "claimant".
-- src:1537 | “claimant” includes a defendant counterclaiming;
@ref s 61(1) claimant (src:1537)
GIVEN `the person is a claimant in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a defendant counterclaiming` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the person is a claimant` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a claimant in the ordinary sense` OR `the person is a defendant counterclaiming`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“claimant” includes a defendant counterclaiming" -- the list is not closed.
            NOTHING

-- s 61(1) "contract of sale".
-- src:1541 | “contract of sale” includes an agreement to sell as well as a sale;
@ref s 61(1) contract of sale (src:1541)
GIVEN `the contract is a sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is an agreement to sell` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the contract is a contract of sale` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract is a sale` OR `the contract is an agreement to sell`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“contract of sale” includes an agreement to sell as well as a sale" -- the list is not closed.
            NOTHING

-- s 61(1) "credit-broker".
-- src:1543 | “credit-broker” means a person acting in the course of a business
-- src:1544 | of credit brokerage carried on by him, that is a business of
-- src:1545 | effecting introductions of individuals desiring to obtain
-- src:1546 | credit —
-- src:1548 | (a) to persons carrying on any business so far as it relates
-- src:1549 | to the provision of credit; or
-- src:1551 | (b) to other persons engaged in credit brokerage;
@ref s 61(1) credit-broker (src:1543-1551)
GIVEN `the person acts in the course of a business of credit brokerage carried on by him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business effects introductions of individuals desiring to obtain credit to persons carrying on any business so far as it relates to the provision of credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business effects introductions of individuals desiring to obtain credit to other persons engaged in credit brokerage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the person is a credit-broker` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person acts in the course of a business of credit brokerage carried on by him` AND (`the business effects introductions of individuals desiring to obtain credit to persons carrying on any business so far as it relates to the provision of credit` OR `the business effects introductions of individuals desiring to obtain credit to other persons engaged in credit brokerage`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“credit-broker” means a person acting in the course of a business of credit brokerage carried on by him, that is a business of effecting introductions of individuals desiring to obtain credit — (a) to persons carrying on any business so far as it relates to the provision of credit; or (b) to other persons engaged in credit brokerage"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 61(1) "delivery".
-- src:1553 | “delivery” means voluntary transfer of possession from one
-- src:1554 | person to another except that, in relation to sections 20A and
-- src:1555 | 20B, it includes such appropriation of goods to the contract as
-- src:1556 | results in property in the goods being transferred to the buyer;
@ref s 61(1) delivery (src:1553-1556)
GIVEN `there is a voluntary transfer of possession from one person to another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question arises in relation to section 20A or 20B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is such appropriation of goods to the contract as results in property in the goods being transferred to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) there is delivery` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is a voluntary transfer of possession from one person to another` OR (`the question arises in relation to section 20A or 20B` AND `there is such appropriation of goods to the contract as results in property in the goods being transferred to the buyer`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“delivery” means voluntary transfer of possession from one person to another except that, in relation to sections 20A and 20B, it includes such appropriation of goods to the contract as results in property in the goods being transferred to the buyer"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 61(1) "document of title to goods".
-- src:1558 | “document of title to goods” has the same meaning as in the
-- src:1559 | Factors Act 1889;
@ref s 61(1) document of title (src:1558-1559)
GIVEN `the Factors Act 1889 treats the document as a document of title to goods` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the document is a document of title to goods` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Factors Act 1889 treats the document as a document of title to goods` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the Factors Act 1889 treats the document as a document of title to goods` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the same meaning as in the Factors Act 1889", and that Act is not among the sources.
            NOTHING

-- s 61(1) "fault".
-- src:1564 | “fault” means wrongful act or default;
@ref s 61(1) fault (src:1564)
GIVEN `the thing is a wrongful act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the thing is fault` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing is a wrongful act` OR `the thing is a default`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“fault” means wrongful act or default"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 61(1) "future goods".
-- src:1566 | “future goods” means goods to be manufactured or acquired by
-- src:1567 | the seller after the making of the contract of sale;
@ref s 61(1) future goods (src:1566-1567)
GIVEN `the goods are to be manufactured by the seller after the making of the contract of sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods are to be acquired by the seller after the making of the contract of sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the goods are future goods` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the goods are to be manufactured by the seller after the making of the contract of sale` OR `the goods are to be acquired by the seller after the making of the contract of sale`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“future goods” means goods to be manufactured or acquired by the seller after the making of the contract of sale"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 61(1) "goods".
-- src:1569 | “goods” includes all personal chattels other than things in action
-- src:1570 | and money; and in particular “goods” includes emblements,
-- src:1571 | industrial growing crops, and things attached to or forming
-- src:1572 | part of the land which are agreed to be severed before sale or
-- src:1573 | under the contract of sale and includes an undivided share in
-- src:1574 | goods;
@ref s 61(1) goods (src:1569-1574)
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A `Kind of thing asked about under the term goods`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the thing is goods` IS
    CONSIDER `the kind of thing`
    WHEN `a personal chattel other than a thing in action or money` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `emblements` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `industrial growing crops` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a thing attached to or forming part of the land which is agreed to be severed before sale or under the contract of sale` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an undivided share in goods` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“goods” includes all personal chattels other than things in action and money" -- an exclusion in the text's own words (reviewer's finding; the earlier reading that "other than" only narrows what is included is withdrawn); the rest of the "includes" definition stays NOTHING below.
    WHEN `a thing in action` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than things in action and money" -- money is named in the same exclusion.
    WHEN `money` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the list is not closed.
    WHEN `some other thing` THEN NOTHING

-- s 61(1) "property".
-- src:1578 | “property” means the general property in goods, and not merely
-- src:1579 | a special property;
@ref s 61(1) property (src:1578-1579)
GIVEN `the interest is the general property in goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the interest is property` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the interest is the general property in goods`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“property” means the general property in goods, and not merely a special property"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 61(1) "sale".
-- src:1581 | “sale” includes a bargain and sale as well as a sale and delivery;
@ref s 61(1) sale (src:1581)
GIVEN `the transaction is a sale and delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is a bargain and sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the transaction is a sale` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the transaction is a sale and delivery` OR `the transaction is a bargain and sale`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“sale” includes a bargain and sale as well as a sale and delivery" -- the list is not closed.
            NOTHING

-- s 61(1) "seller".
-- src:1583 | “seller” means a person who sells or agrees to sell goods;
@ref s 61(1) seller (src:1583)
GIVEN `the person sells goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person agrees to sell goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the person is a seller` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person sells goods` OR `the person agrees to sell goods`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“seller” means a person who sells or agrees to sell goods"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 61(1) "specific goods".
-- src:1585 | “specific goods” means goods identified and agreed on at the
-- src:1586 | time a contract of sale is made and includes an undivided
-- src:1587 | share, specified as a fraction or percentage, of goods
-- src:1588 | identified and agreed on as aforesaid;
@ref s 61(1) specific goods (src:1585-1588)
GIVEN `the goods are identified and agreed on at the time a contract of sale is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is an undivided share, specified as a fraction or percentage, of goods identified and agreed on as aforesaid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the goods are specific goods` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the goods are identified and agreed on at the time a contract of sale is made` OR `the thing is an undivided share, specified as a fraction or percentage, of goods identified and agreed on as aforesaid`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“specific goods” means goods identified and agreed on at the time a contract of sale is made and includes an undivided share, specified as a fraction or percentage, of goods identified and agreed on as aforesaid"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 61(1) "warranty".
-- src:1590 | “warranty” means an agreement with reference to goods which
-- src:1591 | are the subject of a contract of sale, but collateral to the main
-- src:1592 | purpose of such contract, the breach of which gives rise to a
-- src:1593 | claim for damages, but not to a right to reject the goods and
-- src:1594 | treat the contract as repudiated.
@ref s 61(1) warranty (src:1590-1594)
GIVEN `it is an agreement with reference to goods which are the subject of a contract of sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is collateral to the main purpose of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its breach gives rise to a claim for damages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its breach gives rise to a right to reject the goods and treat the contract as repudiated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(1) the agreement is a warranty` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an agreement with reference to goods which are the subject of a contract of sale` AND `it is collateral to the main purpose of the contract` AND `its breach gives rise to a claim for damages` AND (NOT `its breach gives rise to a right to reject the goods and treat the contract as repudiated`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“warranty” means an agreement with reference to goods which are the subject of a contract of sale, but collateral to the main purpose of such contract, the breach of which gives rise to a claim for damages, but not to a right to reject the goods and treat the contract as repudiated"
            JUST FALSE

§§ `The rules of reading in section 61(2) to (5)`

-- s 61(2).
-- src:1596 | (2) A thing is deemed to be done in good faith within the meaning
-- src:1597 | of this Act when it is in fact done honestly, whether it is done
-- src:1598 | negligently or not.
@ref s 61(2) (src:1596-1598)
GIVEN `the thing is in fact done honestly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(2) the thing is deemed to be done in good faith` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing is in fact done honestly`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when it is in fact done honestly" -- a thing not done honestly is not deemed done in good faith ("when" read as "where": fork F10). Whether it was done negligently does not matter, so it is not an input. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (w): "when" read as "where" (ruled 2026-11-05: "when" counts as "where"; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 61(3).
-- src:1600 | (3) A person is deemed to be insolvent within the meaning of this
-- src:1601 | Act if he has either ceased to pay his debts in the ordinary course of
-- src:1602 | business or he cannot pay his debts as they become due.
@ref s 61(3) (src:1600-1602)
GIVEN `he has ceased to pay his debts in the ordinary course of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he cannot pay his debts as they become due` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(3) the person is deemed to be insolvent` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `he has ceased to pay his debts in the ordinary course of business` OR `he cannot pay his debts as they become due`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is deemed to be insolvent within the meaning of this Act if he has either ceased to pay his debts in the ordinary course of business or he cannot pay his debts as they become due."
            -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "if" is read as the text's no; the other reading is that "if" gives a sufficient condition only.
            JUST FALSE

-- s 61(4).
-- src:1604 | (4) Goods are in a deliverable state within the meaning of this Act
-- src:1605 | when they are in such a state that the buyer would under the contract
-- src:1606 | be bound to take delivery of them.
@ref s 61(4) (src:1604-1606)
GIVEN `the goods are in such a state that the buyer would under the contract be bound to take delivery of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(4) the goods are in a deliverable state` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the goods are in such a state that the buyer would under the contract be bound to take delivery of them`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when they are in such a state that the buyer would under the contract be bound to take delivery of them". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (w): "when" read as "where" (ruled 2026-11-05: "when" counts as "where"; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 61(4A).
-- src:1611 | (4A) References in this Act to dealing as consumer are to be
-- src:1612 | construed in accordance with Part 1 of the Unfair Contract Terms
-- src:1613 | Act 1977.
@ref s 61(4A) (src:1611-1613)
GIVEN `Part 1 of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 says the buyer deals as consumer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(4A) the buyer deals as consumer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `Part 1 of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 says the buyer deals as consumer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `Part 1 of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 says the buyer deals as consumer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): references to dealing as consumer "are to be construed in accordance with Part 1 of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977", and that Act is not among the sources.
            NOTHING

-- s 61(4B).
-- src:1615 | (4B) For the purposes of this Act, it is for a seller claiming that the
-- src:1616 | buyer does not deal as consumer to show that he does not.
@ref s 61(4B) (src:1615-1616)
GIVEN `the seller claims that the buyer does not deal as consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller has shown that the buyer does not deal as consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(4B) the seller's claim that the buyer does not deal as consumer is made out` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the seller claims that the buyer does not deal as consumer`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of "a seller claiming that the buyer does not deal as consumer".
            NOTHING
        IF `the seller has shown that the buyer does not deal as consumer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is for a seller claiming that the buyer does not deal as consumer to show that he does not"
            -- MARGINAL (a): a burden rule is read as the text's no when the seller has not shown it; the other reading is that the text says only who must show.
            JUST FALSE

-- s 61(5), paragraph 12.
-- src:1618 | (5) As regards the definition of “business” in subsection (1),
-- src:1619 | paragraph 12 of the Schedule applies in relation to a contract made on
-- src:1620 | or after 18 May 1973 and before 1 February 1978, and paragraph 13
-- src:1621 | in relation to one made before 18 May 1973.
@ref s 61(5) para 12 (src:1618-1621)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(5) paragraph 12 of the Schedule applies as regards the definition of business` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 18 5 1973)) AND (NOT (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 1 2 1978)))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 12 applies "in relation to a contract made on or after 18 May 1973 and before 1 February 1978". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 61(5), paragraph 13.
-- src:1618 | (5) As regards the definition of “business” in subsection (1),
-- src:1619 | paragraph 12 of the Schedule applies in relation to a contract made on
-- src:1620 | or after 18 May 1973 and before 1 February 1978, and paragraph 13
-- src:1621 | in relation to one made before 18 May 1973.
@ref s 61(5) para 13 (src:1618-1621)
GIVEN `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 61(5) paragraph 13 of the Schedule applies as regards the definition of business` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the date the contract was made` AT LEAST (Date 18 5 1973))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph 13 applies "in relation to one made before 18 May 1973". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE
